def methods():
    complete=groups.dropna(subset=['bio1','soc_mean','phh2o_mean'])
    calibration=[]
    for name,label in [('analysis_nitrogen','Nitrogen'),('analysis_remaining','Remaining cycles')]:
        if args.cycle=='N' and name!='analysis_nitrogen':continue
        path=r.parent/name/'calibration_final/final_summary.json'
        if path.exists():
            summary=json.loads(path.read_text())
            passed=[k for k,v in summary['decisions'].items() if v['accepted']]
            calibration.append(label+': '+str(summary['genes'])+' genes; '+str(summary['family_tests'])+' tests. '+('Candidates passing the prespecified gates: '+', '.join(passed)+'. Separate scientific review is still required.' if passed else 'Neither uncertainty method passed every prespecified gate.'))
        elif (r.parent/'reference_calibration.json').exists() and name=='analysis_nitrogen':
            reference=json.loads((r.parent/'reference_calibration.json').read_text())
            assert reference['input_checksums'] and all(hashlib.sha256((r.parent/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==sha for p,sha in reference['input_checksums'].items()), 'Reference calibration input identity changed'
            summary=reference['summary'];passed=[k for k,v in summary['decisions'].items() if v['accepted']]
            calibration.append('Nitrogen: the archived reference calibration used '+str(summary['genes'])+' genes and '+str(summary['family_tests'])+' tests. '+('Candidates passing every gate: '+', '.join(passed)+'.' if passed else 'Neither uncertainty method passed every prespecified gate.')+' This pilot reruns descriptive analyses on verified matching inputs; simulations were not rerun. Archive identity and input checksums are recorded in reference_calibration.json in the download package.')
        else:
            calibration.append(label+': calibration has not been completed for this input release. Historical calibration results are not transferred to these data.')
    return f'''<h3>Input and measurement</h3><p>{n_profiles} WGS profiles are matched by run_accession. Counts are predicted-protein annotation records, not mapped reads, TPM, enzyme concentration, activity or flux. KO representation is divided by total assignments across the full input KO matrix before panel selection and multiplied by one million. An unavailable KO row remains unknown; a zero is an observed non-detection.</p>
<h3>Sampling summaries and environmental diagnostics</h3><p>Runs are averaged within BioSample labels, then BioSample labels are weighted equally within study–coordinate groups. Missing BioSample labels use run-specific fallbacks. Coordinates are rounded to five decimal places for grouping, without increasing their precision. The collection has {len(groups)} descriptive groups at {n_coordinates} coordinates. These labels do not certify independent biological replication.</p><p>Temperature is WorldClim BIO1, in degrees C; organic carbon and pH are SoilGrids 0–5 cm estimates. Stored SoilGrids values are divided by ten in analysis objects. Organic carbon does not measure sediment substrate availability. Complete cases comprise {len(complete)} groups in {complete.study_id.nunique()} study labels. Predictor SDs use ddof=0 before gene-specific positive filtering. OLS slopes describe log2 positive group-mean KO representation, with joint temperature, carbon and pH predictors centred within study. Study-omission ranges are sensitivity ranges, not confidence intervals. A separate diagnostic adds log2 total KO recovery; this is not sequencing depth.</p>
<h3>Calibration and inferential limits</h3><p>{' '.join(calibration)}</p><p>Five mechanisms assess independent errors, study dependence, dominant-study heterogeneity, spatial dependence and heavy tails. Calibration keeps separate nitrogen and remaining-panel test families, uses ddof=1 predictor scales, and evaluates validity, bias, coverage, false positives, FDR and power. The atlas always presents exploratory observed-gene slopes without P or q values. A successful program run or stable slope does not validate ecological inference.</p>
<h3>Biochemical interpretation</h3><p>Arrows indicate reference chemistry, not realized direction or net flux. Shared Mcr, Apr/Dsr, CooS and historical Amo/Pmo annotations retain ambiguity. Community co-detection does not establish complete pathways within organisms. Iron redox and substrate-specific carbohydrate degradation remain unresolved. Sequence-based specialist tools were not rerun. Expand each operational rule to inspect evidence for individual logical blocks, distinguishing detected, not met and unresolvable blocks. Lower and upper block-coverage bounds are not confidence intervals, pathway abundance or organism-level completeness.</p>
<h3>Software actually executed and methods reviewed</h3><p>The atlas is generated by the repository's Python, HTML, CSS and JavaScript code, using NumPy, pandas, Matplotlib and Leaflet. Calibration uses the documented R/Python implementations and clubSandwich reference checks. CNPS.cycle, ggkegg, Escher, MaAsLin 3, adespatial, mgcv, blockCV, METABOLIC, DiTing, DRAM and specialist annotation databases did not generate these observed atlas results. Selected upstream functions were separately tested on synthetic inputs during the implementation audit. Step-based evidence reporting adopts a principle reviewed in METABOLIC and DRAM, with an independent implementation that preserves unknown values. Expand the support table beneath the environmental diagnostics to inspect predictor information after adjustment for the other covariates; information concentration is not an independent sample count or an inferential correction. See the <a href="https://github.com/fjbalvino/mangrove-sediment-biogeography/blob/main/docs/FUNCTIONAL_TOOL_AUDIT.md">versioned implementation audit and adoption decisions</a>.</p>
<h3>Sources and code</h3><ul><li><a href="https://www.kegg.jp/kegg/module.html">KEGG module definitions</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-021-01213-8">METABOLIC</a> · <a href="https://github.com/AnantharamanLab/METABOLIC">code</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/1755-0998.13589">MCycDB</a>; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/nature20152">alkyl-CoM evidence</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/1755-0998.13306">SCycDB</a>; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41396-018-0078-0">Dsr context</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-022-01292-1">PCycDB</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2020.00037">FeGenie</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Arkadiy-Garber/FeGenie">code</a></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad328">dbCAN3</a>; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/srep34212">HydDB</a></li><li><a href="https://jepusto.github.io/clubSandwich/">clubSandwich</a>; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/07350015.2016.1247004">CR2/Satterthwaite</a>; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.8086">simulation reporting</a></li><li><a href="https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html">WorldClim</a>; <a href="https://docs.isric.org/globaldata/soilgrids/SoilGrids_faqs_02.html">SoilGrids units</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/fjbalvino/mangrove-sediment-biogeography/blob/main/docs/GENE_BIOGEOGRAPHY.md">Reproduction guide</a>; <a href="https://github.com/fjbalvino/mangrove-sediment-biogeography/tree/main/scripts/12_gene_environment">analysis and viewer code</a></li></ul>
<h3>Map and visual sources</h3><p>Leaflet 1.9.4 (BSD-2-Clause) is bundled locally. <a href="https://opentopomap.org/">OpenTopoMap</a> tiles use OpenStreetMap and SRTM (CC BY-SA 3.0) and load only for the visible map through native zoom 17. Terrain requires internet and provider availability. The Natural Earth 1:110 million overview and gene controls work offline. Header photograph: <a href="https://www.usgs.gov/media/images/mangroves-and-water">Tracy Enright / USGS</a>, public domain. Map resolution does not improve sample-coordinate accuracy.</p>'''

